## Import deviations

**None.** No import specifier was changed — all copies are byte-identical
to the canonical sources (verified by `cmp`, by `tests/ui-parity.test.ts`
(settings-panel/panel-model/format) and by the workspace drift guard (all 8)).
`version.ts` here is the canonical helper; the public `modelDiscoveryVersion()`
wrapper lives in the repo root `version.ts` and passes this package's own
`package.json` path, so every import and output string is unchanged.

## Recorded deviation: compile-graph exclusion (NOT a content deviation)

`ui/panel-model.ts` is the unadapted control-panel template and imports a
layout this extension does not have:

```
ui/panel-model.ts(1,36): error TS2307: Cannot find module '../config.ts'
ui/panel-model.ts(2,10): error TS2305: Module '"../application.ts"' has no exported member 'ExtensionController'
ui/panel-model.ts(2,31): error TS2305: Module '"../application.ts"' has no exported member 'formatSize'
ui/panel-model.ts(3,33): error TS2307: Cannot find module '../metadata.ts'
```

Chosen fix (keeps byte-identity): `tsconfig.json` excludes `ui/panel-model.ts`
from the compile graph until the model-discovery panel model is adapted onto
it. Nothing imports the file yet, so behavior is unchanged and byte-identity —
not typechecking — is the active guard. The rejected alternative (rewriting
the import specifiers) would have required fabricating `config.ts` /
`metadata.ts` and an `ExtensionController` with delegate-shaped `enabled` /
`mode` / `itemLimit` / `thresholdBytes` settings that model-discovery does
not have.

The other seven vendored files typecheck normally (external peer-deps, zero
cross-file imports, or thin wrappers in this repo's own sources).
